{
  "summary": "Handles cases where an orphan transaction evaluated in a 1P1C package has already entered the mempool via a non-peer pathway such as RPC. Removes an invalid debug assertion that triggered when package evaluation returned a mempool entry status for the child, treating the child as accepted instead.",
  "problem": "Orphan transactions added to the mempool outside peer relay remain in the orphanage until cleaned up. If Find1P1CPackage selects one as a child for a reconsiderable parent, package evaluation returns MEMPOOL_ENTRY for the child and triggers an Assume(false) assertion crash in debug builds.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description and commit b0dda32aff: 'An orphan that enters the mempool other than through peer relay (e.g. by RPC) stays in the orphanage, so Find1P1CPackage can pick it as the child of a reconsiderable parent, and package evaluation then reports it as MEMPOOL_ENTRY, which hit Assume(false). Treat it as accepted instead.'"
  ],
